The plate looks like scrambled egg whites, or possibly crumbled mozzarella. The pieces are white, soft and chunky, which fits cooked egg whites best. The plate is a square, roughly 25 cm across, and the pile covers about half of it, so I'd guess around 150 g.

Cooked egg whites run about 52 kcal per 100 g, so 150 g comes to roughly 78 kcal. If it were mozzarella, 150 g would be about 420 kcal. The texture, with its translucent edges and a few orange flecks, looks more like egg white, though it could be fresh mozzarella or cheese curds. I'll go with egg whites, and since there is some uncertainty, I'll nudge the estimate up slightly.

